 * @remarks Wraps a plain native `<select>` with no custom dropdown/menu markup, so browser-native option rendering and keyboard behavior apply as-is; it shares its field chrome with `text-input`.
 * @selector .pfx-simple-select
 * @modifier -disabled — Disabled state.
 * @modifier -invalid — Invalid (error) state.
 * @modifier -readonly — Read-only state.
 * @modifier -success — Success (valid) state.
 * @modifier -size-sm — Small.
 * @modifier -size-md — (default) Medium.
 * @modifier -size-lg — Large.
 * @pseudo ::placeholder — The placeholder text, in a muted color that shifts on hover.
 * @cssstate disabled
 * @example -canvas-rce
 * <select class="pfx-simple-select">
 *   <option>Choose a fruit…</option>
 *   <option>Apple</option>
 *   <option>Orange</option>
 *   <option>Pear</option>
 * </select>
 * @example -automatica11y
 * ```html
 * <label>Fruit
 *   <select class="pfx-simple-select" data-a11y-trigger data-a11y-root>
 *     <option value="">Choose a fruit</option>
 *     <option value="apple">Apple</option>
 *     <option value="orange">Orange</option>
 *   </select>
